{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He preys on the barren woman</b> — from תרועם (you shall break them). Because he preyed on the barren woman, she does not give birth. And he mentions the barren woman because she has no sons to help her, and the widow who has no husband. Further: he dragged אבירים, mighty men of strength, by his strength — and he knew, when he rises from his bed, that he may die."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:38.214032053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}